   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><br></font><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\">Dear oSCR team,</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\">Im Victor again. I have a question about data entry for oSCR (<span style=\"font-style:italic\">Encounter Data File, EDF)</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><span>This is my question: How to code that an animal </span><b>was detected multiple times</b><span> during the </span><b>same sample occasion</b><span> and </span><b>in the same trap</b><span>?. </span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\">In the toy example below, the same animal (ID=1) was detected 5 times (rows in red) during the same occasion (Sample </font><span style=\"color:rgb(33,53,58);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif;font-size:large\">Occasion =3)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,255);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif;font-size:large\"> and in the same trap (TrapID = 51).</span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\">In my data, I can measure how many times an animal visit a trap during 1 day (1 day of measurement is my unit of sample occasion)</font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><font color=\"#0000ff\">This data entry is OK for oSCR?</font><font color=\"#000000\"></font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#21353a\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">Session ID Occasion trapID </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><font color=\"#0000ce\">1</font><font color=\"#21353a\">,]</font><font color=\"#0000ce\">1 1 1  21 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#ff3333\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">[3,] 1 1 3 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#ff3333\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">[4,] 1 1 3 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#ff3333\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">[5,] 1 1 3 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#ff3333\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">[6,] 1 1 3 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#ff3333\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\">[7,] 1 1 3 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><font color=\"#21353a\">[</font><font color=\"#0000ce\">8</font><font color=\"#21353a\">,]</font><font color=\"#0000ce\">1 1 4 51 </font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font color=\"#0000ce\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><br></font></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\" color=\"#0000ff\"><font><span>How to code this </span></font><span>type of encounter data?.</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in\"><br></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in\"><font size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><font color=\"#0000ce\"><span>Thanks in advance!</span></font><br></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in\"><font color=\"#0000ce\" size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><span><br></span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in\"><font color=\"#0000ce\" size=\"4\" face=\"times new roman, serif\"><span>Victor</span></font></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0.08in;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:-webkit-standard\"><font color=\"#0000ce\"></font></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zlW2w0p8AQAJ",
   "from": "Chris Sutherland",
   "author": "58a62321f08f30f8",
   "date": "2018-09-27T13:12:53Z",
   "subject": "RE: Coding Encounter Data File (EDF)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Hi Victor,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Yes, indeed. You simply provide a row for each observation and if individuals were observed in the same trap and in the same occasion multiple times you would end up with replicate rows. Couple of things:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><span>1.<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">       </span></span></span><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">data2oscr() allows you to set all x&gt;1 values to 0 or retain the frequencies. Specifically, the argument ‘remove.extracaps =’ does this if set to TRUE (which is the default). If set to FALSE, the counts are left as is.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><span>2.<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">       </span></span></span><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">If you keep the counts you will also need to specify this when fitting models. For example, the binomial model (encmod = “B”) is the choice for binary encounter data, while the Poisson model (encmod = “P”) is the choice if you have frequencies.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><span>3.<span style=\"font:7.0pt &quot;Times New Roman&quot;\">       </span></span></span><u></u><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">The interpretation of p0 (which, in hindsight should be called more generally, g0) depends on the encounter model chosen.    <u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\">Chris<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:#000066\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; <b>On Behalf Of </b><a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vma...@fen.uchile.cl</a><br><b>Sent:</b> Monday, September 24, 2018 11:42 AM<br><b>To:</b> oSCR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Subject:</b> Coding Encounter Data File (EDF)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">Dear oSCR team,</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">Im Victor again. I have a question about data entry for oSCR (<i>Encounter Data File, EDF)</i></span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">This is my question: How to code that an animal <b>was detected multiple times</b> during the <b>same sample occasion</b> and <b>in the same trap</b>?. </span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">In the toy example below, the same animal (ID=1) was detected 5 times (rows in red) during the same occasion (Sample </span><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;color:#21353a\">Occasion =3)</span><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;color:blue\"> and in the same trap (TrapID = 51).</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">In my data, I can measure how many times an animal visit a trap during 1 day (1 day of measurement is my unit of sample occasion)</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">This data entry is OK for oSCR?</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#21353a\">Session ID Occasion trapID </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">1</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#21353a\">,]</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">1 1 1  21 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#ff3333\">[3,] 1 1 3 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#ff3333\">[4,] 1 1 3 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#ff3333\">[5,] 1 1 3 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#ff3333\">[6,] 1 1 3 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#ff3333\">[7,] 1 1 3 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#21353a\">[</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">8</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#21353a\">,]</span><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">1 1 4 51 </span><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:blue\">How to code this type of encounter data?.</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">Thanks in advance!</span><u></u><u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:5.75pt\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;color:#0000ce\">Victor</span><u></u><u></u></p></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;oSCR&quot; group.<br>To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_package...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">oscr_p...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>To view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/258272df-22ab-4404-9527-6cc30e307b70%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/258272df-22ab-4404-9527-6cc30e307b70%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492240784000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3-bhrdfNudCsKlQCDqLpS3\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/oscr_package/258272df-22ab-4404-9527-6cc30e307b70%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792492240784000&amp;usg=AOvVaw36GJTxZa6CEg046GGGDZSs\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<u></u><u></u></p></div></div>"
